<title>INDIA: India 97/98 rail budget raises passenger fares.</title>
<headline>India 97/98 rail budget raises passenger fares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Railway Budget for 1997/98 (April-March) on Wednesday proposed an increase of five percent in passenger fares for second class and 10 percent for upper classes.  </p>
<p>The proposed hike in passenger fares is expected to fetch 18 billion rupees ($503 million) during 1997/98.</p>
<p>The increased passenger fares will come into effect from April 1.</p>
<p>The budget also proposed to impose a 20 percent surcharge on parcels and luggage booked on superfast trains.</p>
<p>But there will no increase in passenger fares in season tickets for second and upper class. ($1 = 35.8 rupees)</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsrrom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
